# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression list
# Add one CVE-ID per line to suppress accepted-risk findings.
# Each entry MUST include a justification comment and review date.

# CVE-2026-35568 — MCP Core DNS rebinding vulnerability
# Fix available in mcp-core:1.0.0 but 0.18.x/1.0.0 removed McpJsonMapper.createDefault(),
# breaking mcp-annotations:0.8.0 used by Spring AI 1.1.4. Pinned to 0.17.2 deliberately.
# Accepted risk: DNS rebinding requires attacker on the same network segment.
# Review when Spring AI upgrades to mcp-annotations compatible with SDK ≥1.0.0.
CVE-2026-35568

# CVE-2026-34483 — Tomcat information disclosure via JsonAccessLogValve encoding
# CVE-2026-34487 — Tomcat information disclosure via sensitive data in log files
# Both fixed in Tomcat 10.1.54 / 11.0.21. Spring Boot 3.5.13 (latest) ships 10.1.53.
# No Spring Boot patch available yet. Remove when Boot 3.5.14+ (Tomcat 10.1.54+) is released.
# Review: 2026-05-01
CVE-2026-34483
CVE-2026-34487
